---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Affiliate Disclosure | MyRigFoundry"
  description="Learn how affiliate links and product recommendations may be used on MyRigFoundry."
>
  <section class="info-page">
    <div class="info-container">
      <p class="eyebrow">AFFILIATE DISCLOSURE</p>

      <h1>How affiliate links work on MyRigFoundry.</h1>

      <p class="info-lead">
        Some pages on MyRigFoundry may contain affiliate links. This page
        explains what that means and how those links relate to our editorial
        content.
      </p>

      <div class="info-content">
        <h2>What is an affiliate link?</h2>

        <p>
          An affiliate link is a link to a product or service that may allow
          MyRigFoundry to earn a commission when a reader makes a qualifying
          purchase or completes another eligible action through that link.
        </p>

        <p>
          Using an affiliate link does not normally change the price paid by
          the reader.
        </p>

        <h2>Recommendations come first</h2>

        <p>
          Affiliate commissions do not determine whether a product should be
          recommended.
        </p>

        <p>
          Our goal is to recommend hardware only when it is relevant to the
          problem being discussed and when purchasing something may genuinely
          make sense.
        </p>

        <p>
          If a problem can reasonably be solved through troubleshooting
          without buying new hardware, our guides should make that clear.
        </p>

        <h2>Affiliate relationships</h2>

        <p>
          MyRigFoundry may participate in affiliate programs offered by
          retailers, manufacturers or other technology-related companies.
        </p>

        <p>
          When affiliate links are used, we aim to disclose that relationship
          clearly so readers can understand when MyRigFoundry may receive
          compensation.
        </p>

        <h2>Editorial independence</h2>

        <p>
          Compensation, affiliate availability or potential commission should
          not change our technical conclusions about a product or PC problem.
        </p>

        <p>
          Product recommendations may also change over time as hardware,
          pricing, availability and better alternatives change.
        </p>

        <div class="article-note">
          <strong>Transparency matters</strong>

          The purpose of affiliate monetization is to support MyRigFoundry
          while keeping troubleshooting guides and educational content
          available to readers.
        </div>

        <h2>Questions</h2>

        <p>
          Questions about affiliate relationships or disclosures can be sent
          through our <a href="/contact/">Contact page</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>